commit 77b4f0ba2cd160b5b656e4e8344886f919021a9c
Author: mbvgua <mbvgua+dev@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 18 22:24:51 2026 +0300

    feat(sqlite): added sqlite as a database
    
    CHANGES:
    - was previously storing data in a python list, which does not scale or
      persist across session. added a simple Sqlite database, which helped
      me get into app modularization, database relationships and models,
      better api design and such.
    - the sqlite db persists across sessions, which is more prod ready.
      also, using a SQLAlchemy ORM allows one to easily patch in any
      database oftheir choosing(sqlite, mysql, mariadb, postgres and such).
      I really liked working with raw sql dues to stored procedures,
      triggers and such, but I can see mysqlf working with an ORM just for
      the plug and play fatures here
    
    CONSIDERATIONS:
    - figure out how to create stored procedures and triggers in an ORM,
      moreso the SQLAlchemy ORM.

